{
  "analysis": "I'm in the /workspace directory and can see several files and directories: gen_inputs.py, references directory, setup.sh, and skill_context directory. I need to explore these to understand the agent routing system and what needs to be created for the sap-helper sub-agent.",
  "plan": "First, I'll explore the directory structure to understand what's available. I'll start by listing the contents of the references and skill_context directories, then read the relevant files to understand the existing agent routing patterns.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la references/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la skill_context/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "I can see there's a references directory with agent-registry.json and task-routing-rules.md, and a skill_context directory with SKILL.md and manifest.json. I need to read these files to understand the existing agent routing patterns before creating the sap-helper agent.",
  "plan": "Read the key files to understand the agent routing system: agent-registry.json, task-routing-rules.md, SKILL.md, and manifest.json. Also check the skill_context/references subdirectory.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat references/agent-registry.json\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat references/task-routing-rules.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/SKILL.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/manifest.json\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la skill_context/references/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "I've gathered key information:\n1. agent-registry.json has one agent 'main' (Clawdia) that reports to human 'Ilkerkaan', has empty can_assign_to, and requires_approval: false\n2. task-routing-rules.md notes SAP work should be delegated to a specialized agent\n3. SKILL.md describes the agents-manager skill with rules about discovery, permission checks, and a Handshake Protocol\n4. The manifest.json shows this is the 'agents-manager' skill\n\nI need to see more of the SKILL.md content and check the skill_context/references directory.",
  "plan": "Read the rest of SKILL.md and check skill_context/references for any additional routing examples or templates. Then I'll create the sap-helper agent spec and update the registry.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/SKILL.md | head -200\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la skill_context/references/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/references/*\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "I can see the SKILL.md has important routing rules: the Handshake Protocol checks requires_approval before assigning. If FALSE, assign directly; if TRUE, ask supervisor first. I need to see more of the SKILL.md to find examples of agent configurations and check the skill_context/references directory.",
  "plan": "Read more of SKILL.md to find agent configuration examples, then check the skill_context/references directory for any templates or examples.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/SKILL.md | tail -200\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls skill_context/references/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "I've seen the core routing rules. The Handshake Protocol is key: if requires_approval is FALSE, assign directly; if TRUE, ask supervisor first. I need to see more of SKILL.md to find agent configuration examples and check skill_context/references for templates.",
  "plan": "Read the middle section of SKILL.md where agent configuration examples might be, and list contents of skill_context/references directory.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/SKILL.md | sed -n '100,300p'\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la skill_context/references/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "Found additional reference files in skill_context/references/: agent-profile-schema.md, agent-registry.md, and task-routing-rules.md. These will help me understand the exact format needed for the sap-helper agent configuration.",
  "plan": "Read all three reference files to understand the agent profile schema, registry format, and routing rules in detail.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/references/agent-profile-schema.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/references/agent-registry.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/references/task-routing-rules.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "I've seen the agent-profile-schema.md which shows the structure. Key fields include: id, name, model, capabilities, requires_approval (default true), auto_accept_from, can_assign_to, reports_to, escalation_path, and agent_card. Now I need to see the agent-registry.md and task-routing-rules.md for examples.",
  "plan": "Read the agent-registry.md and task-routing-rules.md files to see complete examples of agent configurations and routing rules.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/references/agent-registry.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/references/task-routing-rules.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "I've seen the agent-registry.md with the main agent (Clawdia) configuration. Now I need to read the task-routing-rules.md to understand the complete routing rules before creating the sap-helper agent.",
  "plan": "Read the task-routing-rules.md file to understand routing rules, then I'll have all the information needed to create the sap-helper agent spec and update the registry.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/references/task-routing-rules.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "Successfully created the sap-helper-spec.yaml file. Now I need to update the agent-registry.json to add the sap-helper agent and update main's can_assign_to list to include sap-helper.",
  "plan": "1. Read the current agent-registry.json to understand its exact structure\n2. Update agent-registry.json to add sap-helper and update main's can_assign_to\n3. Create the handoff note",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat references/agent-registry.json\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "I can see the current agent-registry.json structure. I need to update it to add the sap-helper agent and update main's can_assign_to list to include 'sap-helper'. The sap-helper should have requires_approval: true (for non-auto-approved tasks) and auto_accept_from: ['main'] so tasks from main are auto-approved.",
  "plan": "Update agent-registry.json with the sap-helper agent entry and update main's can_assign_to to include sap-helper.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat > references/agent-registry.json << 'EOF'
{
  "agents": [
    {
      "id": "main",
      "name": "Clawdia",
      "model": "glm-4.7",
      "reports_to": {
        "type": "human",
        "target": "Ilkerkaan"
      },
      "can_assign_to": ["sap-helper"],
      "requires_approval": false,
      "agent_card": {
        "id": "main",
        "name": "Clawdia",
        "description": "Main orchestrator agent.",
        "capabilities": [
          "general assistance",
          "task routing"
        ],
        "input_format": "Natural language",
        "output_format": "Plain text",
        "routing": {
          "reports_to": "Ilkerkaan",
          "can_assign_to": ["sap-helper"]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "sap-helper",
      "name": "SAP Helper",
      "model": "glm-4.7",
      "reports_to": {
        "type": "human",
        "target": "Ilkerkaan"
      },
      "can_assign_to": [],
      "requires_approval": true,
      "auto_accept_from": ["main"],
      "agent_card": {
        "id": "sap-helper",
        "name": "SAP Helper",
        "description": "Specialized sub-agent for SAP-related tasks including ABAP, FI/CO, MM, SD, and S/4HANA.",
        "capabilities": [
          "SAP system administration",
          "ABAP development",
          "SAP module support (FI/CO/MM/SD)",
          "S/4HANA configuration",
          "BAPI/IDoc integration"
        ],
        "input_format": "Natural language with SAP context",
        "output_format": "Plain text with SAP-specific terminology",
        "routing": {
          "reports_to": "Ilkerkaan (human)",
          "can_assign_to": [],
          "auto_accept_from": ["main"]
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
EOF
",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ]
}

